WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.657
In this video, you design the tabs and sections that a workspace shows on an

1.2
00:00:05.657 --> 00:00:08.361
encounter. Step 1. Open the workspace.

1.3
00:00:08.361 --> 00:00:13.842
To find a Draft workspace, select the Draft tab, then select its name.

2.1
00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:19.395
Step 2. Choose a starter. Blank gives one empty tab named Overview.

2.2
00:00:19.395 --> 00:00:23.931
A starter changes nothing for users until you save.

3.1
00:00:23.931 --> 00:00:27.614
Step 3. Arrange the tabs. Select Add tab.

3.2
00:00:27.614 --> 00:00:33.308
Under Built-in tabs, you can add a standard Care tab, such as Notes.

3.3
00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:36.571
A lock icon marks a built-in tab.

4.1
00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:42.193
Step 4. Choose the layout of a tab. In the Layout row, select a layout.

4.2
00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:47.610
Main plus side gives a wide Main column and a narrow Side column.

5.1
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:53.252
Step 5. Add sections. At the bottom of a column, select Add a section.

5.2
00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:56.564
To find a section, type in Search sections.

5.3
00:00:56.564 --> 00:01:03.239
Select the section, and Care adds it to that column.

6.1
00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:09.338
Step 6. Arrange the sections. Drag a section to another place or column.

6.2
00:01:09.338 --> 00:01:15.281
Or select its three-dot button, then Move up, Move down or Move to.

7.1
00:01:15.281 --> 00:01:21.354
Step 7. Preview the design. The canvas uses sample content, not patient records.

7.2
00:01:21.354 --> 00:01:27.604
Select Closed encounter to see which sections hide when an encounter is closed.

8.1
00:01:27.604 --> 00:01:33.717
Step 9. Save the design. Select Save Changes. Care shows Workspace updated.

8.2
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:39.455
If the workspace is Active, people who chose it see the new design.
